      "writtenOn": "2023-02-17T16:39:15Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This is probably a good change to make (if also changing all the others here, or removing them). However, this means that the `--nonativeFonts` flag no longer works the way it used to. Before this just looked to the default `SkFontMgr` for creating a typeface from a stream, so setting it the the test font manager was enough to prevent any OpenType data from being interpreted. However, this now looks though all the registered factories, so if we built in some handler (FreeType, CoreText, or DirectWrite) then it will be used.",
      "revId": "70ab605173e4eb94f8e1b93b176dd6688a18abeb",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
